Our bank invests in syndicated loans and bonds. Typically the borrower of such syndicated loan or bond is an (intermediate) holding company of a larger group of entities (‘borrower group’), whereby the loan is guaranteed by companies in the group that operate the business activities. The guarantee is irrevocable, unconditional, joint and several.  In the case of bonds SPEs can also be created by the borrowers for the purposes of financing. In case of default we can address to any Guarantor of the borrowing group to be repaid the full amount of loan. Besides, the decision to invest in the loan or in security is based on assessment of activities of the entire borrower group and not on the immediate borrower.

